Nicely and creepily done, though from a game called "Dream" I expected more than just flying cubes and maze puzzles (no worries, they stop and go into adventure game mode);
I really want to warn you NOT to get this game but it would seem that's because of my mindset; So I will recommend it, BUT:
DO NOT expect psychedelic ideas or imagery from this; This is _VERY_ conventional. It's nicely done, it has atmosphere and can be creepy, but it's _conventional_; It does nothing _new_. It does not warp reality, formality or your mind;
If you're into decent semi-atmospheric adventures\puzzles -- go for it!

