TL;DR: Co-op in this game is awesome!
If you have someone who share your passion with turn based combat RPGs, this co-op gem is for you two. The game has everything I ever wanted from this genre, and you should check my to-do list for this game:
- Loot every house you encounter;
- Farm every mob pack on the map;
- Explore every nuke and cranny!
Combat is quite tactical, there's a lot of control going on in each encounter. Spells interact with each other which is one of the selling points. For example:
- Detonate poisonous gas clouds, leaving a thick cloud of smoke so archers can't aim through it;
- Freeze the ground so enemies running through it will slip and fall flat on their faces (even the big ones which is amusing as all hell!);
- Make it raing and then stun foes with lightning strikes, and many more.
Split-screen with controllers available, and it's passable. Not as natural as kbm controls but not cringe worthy.
It was something between 9/10 and 10/10 for me, but now I grasped the enchancements of Original Sin 2 (Gog version), and it patched every flaw ths one has.

